  "minutes": 35,
  "recap": "Welcome to Day 19 of Quantitative & Low-Latency Systems Engineering. On Day 18, we mastered multidimensional Kalman filtering to continuously neutralize dynamic multi-asset beta. However, when placing limit orders at the National Best Bid or Offer (NBBO) to earn the bid-ask spread, executing passively requires waiting in an electronic limit order queue. In Price-Time Priority (FIFO) matching engines, knowing your exact position in the queue is the difference between earning profitable passive rebates and suffering toxic adverse selection fills. Today, we build the institutional FIFO Queue Position Estimator.",
