        "While Tier 2 provides real-time probabilistic risk estimates, Tier 3 introduces rigorous higher-moment adjustments and large-scale simulation capabilities: the Correlated Monte Carlo & Cornish-Fisher Stress Engine. In complex quantitative portfolios, market returns exhibit significant third-moment asymmetry (negative skewness S) and fourth-moment fat tails (excess kurtosis K). If a risk platform ignores these higher moments, it will severely underestimate the probability of joint multi-asset market dislocations.",
